-- chem/facts.cub — relative facts and stable facts (Rovelli, relational quantum mechanics, 1996; Di Biagio
-- and Rovelli, "Stable facts, relative facts", 2021), in Part I's terms. There is no absolute state: a
-- fact is a reading of the world relative to the system that holds it, an observation o : H → O, and
-- what the fact leaves open is its fiber (1.1). A fact of one system is stable for another when the other's
-- record fixes it — when it factors through what the other holds — which is what decoherence with an
-- environment produces. A fold is such a fact: stable for the solvent and for every apparatus that records
-- the chain afterwards, so what one experiment reports of it is what every other must.
import "fold.hypercubical"

